<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan re-enters MTBE market for March supplies.</title>
<headline>Taiwan re-enters MTBE market for March supplies.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has re-entered the methyl tertiary butyl ether (MTBE) after a two-month absence, a a company official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender which seeks cargoes for March 1-15 delivery on a cost-and-freight (c-and-f) basis to Kaohsiung and/or Keelung closes January 22 and is valid for two days, sources said.</p>
<p>The official said CPC's did not enter the spot market for January or February requirements as it was committed on term supplies.</p>
<p>CPC's total monthly demand ranges between four to six cargoes, the official said.</p>
<p>CPC's last MTBE purchase, for December 1-15 delivery to Kaohsiung or Taichung was at $275-$278 per tonne, c-and-f.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
</text>
